: "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CY6V9qMTQeKSZYdVcEJaue", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376320, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CY6V9qMTQeKSZYdVcEJaue", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 380722, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212), which is what `tests/test_money.py` checks.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change, made in commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on that commit passed.\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 in the advisory system to confirm the rule, but it came back as unknown. The fix is based on what the test and the docstring both say.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FbLwtN9jiQ1NbsMZNfUqhW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011jTArLfAHzNvuqgu97UbYy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Jgf5rgC11LCLHTkBoLdjBQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "tool